    {
      "id": "RYIaJ_3GsxWjHNIP5mZqA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 48.061941024947146,
      "y": 681.5638755837939,
      "width": 653.7998657226562,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "am",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1449319829,
      "version": 1302,
      "versionNonce": 818288053,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1736014299844,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "So the first thing that comes to our mind is \nusing a HashTable. \n-> using a HashTable can provide for a very efficient retrieval \nand addition of data.\n-> Provide us the GET and PUT functionality which is needed. \n\nBut one challenge with the hashTable is that, the keys for the \nhashtable will be limited. and we can't really have all the data into\nthe cache and like we discussed in requirement. \n-> and we know that caches are really really expensive, so what we\n    can do is we can consider CACHE POLICIES into account \n\n-> cache policy -> how much data will be stored in the cache &\n        how we're going to evict the data from the cache\n        -> one of the eviction policy is like LRU, LFU FIFO\n\nbut how do we take care of the policy since we're only dealing with\nthe Hashtable. \n\n----- EXPLAIN LRU CACHE ----",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "So the first thing that comes to our mind is \nusing a HashTable. \n-> using a HashTable can provide for a very efficient retrieval \nand addition of data.\n-> Provide us the GET and PUT functionality which is needed. \n\nBut one challenge with the hashTable is that, the keys for the \nhashtable will be limited. and we can't really have all the data into\nthe cache and like we discussed in requirement. \n-> and we know that caches are really really expensive, so what we\n    can do is we can consider CACHE POLICIES into account \n\n-> cache policy -> how much data will be stored in the cache &\n        how we're going to evict the data from the cache\n        -> one of the eviction policy is like LRU, LFU FIFO\n\nbut how do we take care of the policy since we're only dealing with\nthe Hashtable. \n\n----- EXPLAIN LRU CACHE ----",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
