    {
      "id": "8JM16TnVNRWRLrOLeo9_1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 776.979443141407,
      "y": 714.395530240037,
      "width": 738.3399047851562,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b01",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 345521173,
      "version": 1350,
      "versionNonce": 473261877,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1736016904069,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "so now we've two caches. \n#1 approach is that we can have them deplyoed in the same host\nbenefit - since same host - avoiding maintenance overhead, it scales\nautomatically with the Service. \nchallenge - if something happens to Host-A, service B won't be able\nto access the Cache \n#2 is that we deploy everything in their own host, revolves the issue\nbut too much overhead. but we get a plus point that we can independently \nscale the caches. \n\nBased on these two approaches we can decide what do to. BUT \nstill the main question remains. that how are we going to take care of the \nwhich Cache to select ?  \n\n- Naive way\n---- DISCUSS MOD, HASHING AND  HASH_FUNCTION\n-- better approach \n---- EXPLAIN CONSISTENT HASHING ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "so now we've two caches. \n#1 approach is that we can have them deplyoed in the same host\nbenefit - since same host - avoiding maintenance overhead, it scales\nautomatically with the Service. \nchallenge - if something happens to Host-A, service B won't be able\nto access the Cache \n#2 is that we deploy everything in their own host, revolves the issue\nbut too much overhead. but we get a plus point that we can independently \nscale the caches. \n\nBased on these two approaches we can decide what do to. BUT \nstill the main question remains. that how are we going to take care of the \nwhich Cache to select ?  \n\n- Naive way\n---- DISCUSS MOD, HASHING AND  HASH_FUNCTION\n-- better approach \n---- EXPLAIN CONSISTENT HASHING ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
